Self-Test
Test Your Understanding
Answer these before your training session (to check your pre-read comprehension) and again after (to test retention). Click an option to check your answer.

Q1. A JD arrives with 14 listed requirements. What is your first action?
Source against all 14 requirements — the JD is the final word on what the client wants.
Assume inflation. Apply the 80/20 rule and confirm the real deal-breakers with manager before sourcing.
Ask the candidate which skills they have before deciding.
Q2. The JD says "MUST HAVE SPRING BOOT — NO EXCEPTIONS" in the middle of a paragraph dump. What does this tell you?
It's a formatting error — ignore the CAPS LOCK text.
This is a hiring manager comment — Spring Boot is the deal-breaker that will cause immediate rejection if missing.
Spring Boot is probably just a nice-to-have preference.
Q3. "Strong communication skills" appears in the requirements section. You should:
Include it as a Boolean keyword — it's in the required section.
Screen out candidates who don't explicitly list communication skills on their resume.
Translate it by looking at responsibilities for the actual communication context — assess it on the screening call, not in your Boolean string.
Q4. The difference between a Job Description (JD) and a Job Requisition (Req) is:
They are the same document with different names.
The JD describes the role. The Req is the financial/business approval to hire — contains budget, rate, and timeline.
The JD is only for the candidate to read; the req is the recruiter's private document.
Q5. When building the TSTE table, the "Research" row is for:
Researching the candidate's background and LinkedIn profile.
Finding co-occurring skills and vocabulary that candidates actually use — to build a more complete Boolean search than just copying the JD.
Researching the client company's industry background.
Q6. "ServiceNow" in a job description is classified as a:
Hard skill — it's a technical requirement
Soft skill — it involves how people work together
Tool — it's a specific software platform used in the role
